# `.env.example` (template — DO NOT add real values)

> **Note:** FinPlan Pro is **offline-first**. There is no `.env` file in this repo, by design. The app does not connect to any external service, has no API keys, no telemetry, and no cloud URLs.
>
> If you fork the app and add a remote backend, drop your env vars here and update `docs/tech-stack.md` and `docs/security-guidelines.md` accordingly.

---

## Build / Bundle

```ini
# Set to "true" to emit bundle-report/stats.html on next `vite build`
ANALYZE=

# Override the default Vite port (5173, strictPort)
PORT=

# Override the default public path for static assets
BASE_URL=/
```

## Tauri (optional desktop build)

```ini
# Tauri CLI auto-detects these. Uncomment to override.
# TAURI_DEV_HOST=
# TAURI_DEV_PORT=
# TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY=
# TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD=
```

## Linting / Testing

```ini
# Set to "true" to skip the 80GB `--max-old-space-size=81920` heap override
SKIP_HEAP_OVERRIDE=

# Vitest reporter override (default / spec / verbose / json)
VITEST_REPORTER=
```

## Plugin Marketplace (only if self-hosting)

```ini
# URL of a self-hosted plugin marketplace JSON feed (defaults to local /plugins)
# PLUGIN_MARKETPLACE_URL=
```

## Telemetry / Crash Reporting (intentionally NOT included)

```ini
# This project does NOT collect telemetry. Do not add:
#   SENTRY_DSN=
#   POSTHOG_KEY=
#   AMPLITUDE_API_KEY=
# Adding any of the above would violate the offline-first design contract.
```

---

## Verification

```bash
# Confirm no .env is present (should output nothing)
ls -la .env .env.local .env.production 2>/dev/null || echo "OK: no .env files"

# Confirm Vite still builds without env vars
node node_modules/.bin/vite build
```

> ⚠️ **If you add real environment variables**, ensure they are NOT committed. Add `.env*` to `.gitignore` (currently the repo has no `.env*` files, so `.gitignore` is implicit). Update this file and the project docs in the same PR.
